The plugin bundles buzz-app modules unchanged at the revision in
src/constants.ts (BUZZ_APP_REV), among them the Goose agent type's runtime,
run wiring and synced settings (src/bundled/goose/runtime.ts, run.ts and
settings.ts). The build puts two files of this plugin in place of two Goose
modules (vite.config.ts, SWAPS). These files adapt buzz-app code from its
bundled Goose agent type; each names its source in a header comment:

- src/opencode.ts: replaces src/bundled/goose/goose.ts and keeps its export
  names; its hooks follow that file.
- src/sessions.ts: replaces src/bundled/goose/sessions.ts; from that file.
- src/setup.ts: reading thinking levels follows src/bundled/goose/setup.ts.
- src/provider.tsx: the provider dialog and default control follow
  src/bundled/goose/tabs.tsx, built from the same buzz-app components.
- src/activity.tsx: the Activity tab follows src/bundled/goose/tabs.tsx, built
  from the same buzz-app components.
- src/session-read.ts: reading sessions from the harness, their limits and the
  first-prompt check follow src/bundled/goose/transcript.ts; shared with this
  project's other ACP plugin.
- src/transcript.ts: turns from a replay follow src/bundled/goose/transcript.ts;
  shared with this project's other ACP plugin.
- src/index.ts: the agent type wiring follows src/bundled/goose/index.ts.
- src/views.tsx: the New agent and Settings views follow
  src/bundled/goose/tabs.tsx, built from the same buzz-app components.

The build also bundles react-markdown and remark-gfm, with the unified, micromark
and mdast libraries they use, for the transcripts. Each is licensed under the
MIT License (@ungap/structured-clone: ISC).

OpenCode is a separate program by its own authors (https://opencode.ai).
This plugin does not include it; it starts the copy the user installed.

src/icon.tsx and icon.png draw the OpenCode mark from OpenCode's favicon
(packages/app/public/favicon-v3.svg in https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode),
with rounded tile corners. That file is licensed under the MIT License:

